     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\">Hi D-RUGies,</font></span><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\">A bit late, but here&#39;s your reminder that our weekly work session is on for tomorrow at 10am, in the <a href=\"http://dsi.ucdavis.edu/directions.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://dsi.ucdavis.edu/directions.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466704801000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3CLr87UXo8nBl59cYYACdD\">DSI (360 Shields</a>). Bring your questions/work and enjoy the space.</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><u><b><font face=\"georgia, serif\">PACKAGE OF THE WEEK:</font></b></u></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Currently there are <b>11, 597</b> </span>total packages on <a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;text-decoration-line:none;color:rgb(102,17,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466704801000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0uhwM1C98e0iz7gvEjgUsW\">CRAN</a>. This week a package I&#39;d like to put out in the ether is </font><font face=\"monospace, monospace\"><b><a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/riverdist/index.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/riverdist/index.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466704801000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3r2b0U9TMB8ZZ8miUl6aC4\">riverdist</a>. </b></font><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Times;font-size:medium\"><i>Reads river network shape files and computes network distances. Also included are a variety of computation and graphical tools designed for fisheries telemetry research, such as minimum home range, kernel density estimation, and clustering analysis using empirical k-functions with a bootstrap envelope. Tools are also provided for editing the river networks, meaning there is no reliance on external software.</i></span></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\">If you have a package you really enjoy using that&#39;s a hidden gem, or a fun new package you just discovered, etc., please send them my way! I&#39;d prefer to try to focus on the packages that are a bit outside of the core/popular packages folks use (i.e., tidyverse, lattice, etc), but happy to take whatever feedback you all have. Ultimately I just want a sentence or two about the package or how you use it, a link to the vignette, and call it good. Here&#39;s a google form we can use to compile all of these:</font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><br></font></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-size:13px\"><ul><li style=\"line-height:17px\"><font face=\"georgia, serif\"><a href=\"https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;text-decoration-line:none;color:rgb(102,17,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466704802000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0YmiMUauHuWxr__PuUrD1b\">https://goo.gl/forms/VzzeldnaEOkNImJ73</a><br></font></li></ul><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><br></div><ul style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\"><li style=\"line-height:17px\"><b><i>SPYvsSPY</i></b><span style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">: For this week, I&#39;ll mention a recent CRAN addition that catalogues data from all the Spy vs. Spy comics (from MAD Magazine). Sort of a fun dataset for statistical examples or just playing around with. It&#39;s on CRAN, and on github </span><a href=\"https://github.com/shabbychef/SPYvsSPY\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;text-decoration-line:none;color:rgb(102,17,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/shabbychef/SPYvsSPY&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792466704802000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ajn4Qb_z2g5SdtBYfxDNf\">here</a>.</li></ul></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Adios,<br></div><div style=\"margin:0px;padding:0px;border:0px\">Ryan</div></div><div><br></div>-- <br><div class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><br><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;float:none;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline\"><span> </span></span><br style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"></b></i></font></span><div style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px\"><font size=\"1\"><i>&quot;When we try to pick out anything by itself, we find it hitched to everything else in the universe.&quot;<b><br>John Muir (My First Summer in the Sierra, 1911)</b></i></font></div><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><i><b>-----------------------------------------------------</b></i></font></span></div><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-style:normal;font-variant-ligatures:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;line-height:19px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><font face=\"times new roman, serif\"><div>Ryan Peek</div><div>PhD Candidate, Graduate Group in Ecology<br></div><div dir=\"ltr\">Center for Watershed Sciences, UC Davis</div></font></span><div style=\"font-family:arial;font-size:small;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span style=\"line-height:19px\"><div><b style=\"color:rgb(11,83,148);font-family:&quot;times new roman&quot;